 ## Operating characteristics
 
 ### Time and Memory Complexity
-*   **Time:** The complexity is dominated by the root-finding operation for surface depth for each sampled pixel $N_p$. This typically involves multiple queries to the occupancy network $f_\theta$. The number of queries depends on the precision of the root-finding algorithm (e.g., binary search iterations). The loss computation itself is $O(N_p)$ [S1][S2, unofficial].
-*   **Memory:** Memory usage is proportional to $N_p$ for storing sampled points, depths, and intermediate gradients. The network parameters are stored separately [S1][S2, unofficial].
+*   **Time:** The complexity is dominated by the root-finding operation for surface depth for each sampled pixel $N_p$. The loss computation itself scales linearly with the number of sampled pixels [G].
